  m_Name: Blade17
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Blade (2)
  description: The Blade (2) plays a vital role in the jet engine's compression process,
    working in tandem with other blades to increase the air pressure and temperature
    before it enters the combustion chamber. Its position and shape are carefully
    designed to minimize energy losses and maximize airflow, making it an essential
    component of the engine's efficiency. Notably, the Blade (2) is often coated
    with a thin layer of protective material to reduce wear and tear from the high-velocity
    air flowing over it.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3095557998d7d8c418190525a441d886, type: 3}
